From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AllocatorHooks: do not lock rpmalloc for libc size queries

The disabled-allocator malloc_usable_size implementation calls
IOS_RPM_GUARD even though that macro is defined only in the enabled
rpmalloc branch. This prevents the native JemallocDummy target from
building with ENABLE_FEX_ALLOCATOR=OFF.

Remove the stray guard from the libc-backed implementation, matching the
other libc hooks. Keep all enabled-allocator guards unchanged: libc size
queries do not access rpmalloc state and must not acquire its iOS lock.

Class: build-fix
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-01-fex-native-allocator.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 FEXCore/Source/Utils/AllocatorHooks.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Utils/AllocatorHooks.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Utils/AllocatorHooks.cpp
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Utils/AllocatorHooks.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Utils/AllocatorHooks.cpp
@@ -290,7 +290,6 @@ void free(void* ptr) {
   return ::free(ptr);
 }
 size_t malloc_usable_size(void* ptr) {
-  IOS_RPM_GUARD();
 #ifdef __APPLE__
   return ::malloc_size(ptr);
 #else
